ee4f4e66 (Oliver Butterley 2025-06-02 21:49:31 +0200  3) -- To go in `Logic/Function/Iterate`? Name as `iterate_of_invariant`?
c6f6cb89 (Lua V. R.        2024-06-23 21:27:13 -0300  4) /-- If a function `φ` is invariant under a function `f` (i.e., `φ ∘ f = φ`),
524bd3a7 (Pietro Monticone 2024-06-24 00:20:49 +0200  5) then `φ` remains invariant under any number of iterations of `f`. -/
80d55054 (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 15:49:42 -0300  6) lemma invariant_iter (h : φ ∘ f = φ) : ∀ i, φ ∘ f^[i] = φ
80d55054 (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 15:49:42 -0300  7)   | 0 => rfl
80d55054 (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 15:49:42 -0300  8)   | n + 1 => by
80d55054 (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 15:49:42 -0300  9)     change (φ ∘ f^[n]) ∘ f = φ
80d55054 (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 15:49:42 -0300 10)     rwa [invariant_iter h n]
80d55054 (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 15:49:42 -0300 11) 
ee4f4e66 (Oliver Butterley 2025-06-02 21:49:31 +0200 12) -- To go in `Dynamics/BirkhoffSum/Basic`
a62a5c5f (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 03:54:09 -0300 13) open Finset in
c6f6cb89 (Lua V. R.        2024-06-23 21:27:13 -0300 14) /-- If a function `φ` is invariant under a function `f` (i.e., `φ ∘ f = φ`),
c6f6cb89 (Lua V. R.        2024-06-23 21:27:13 -0300 15) then the Birkhoff sum of `φ` over `f` for `n` iterations is equal to `n • φ`. -/
ee4f4e66 (Oliver Butterley 2025-06-02 21:49:31 +0200 16) theorem birkhoffSum_of_invariant [AddCommMonoid M] {φ : α → M}
a62a5c5f (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 03:54:09 -0300 17)     (h : φ ∘ f = φ) : birkhoffSum f φ n = n • φ := by
80d55054 (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 15:49:42 -0300 18)   funext x
80d55054 (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 15:49:42 -0300 19)   unfold birkhoffSum
80d55054 (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 15:49:42 -0300 20)   conv in fun _ => _ => intro k; change (φ ∘ f^[k]) x; rw [invariant_iter h k]
80d55054 (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 15:49:42 -0300 21)   simp
a62a5c5f (Lua V. R.        2024-05-27 03:54:09 -0300 22) 
